+# The Daily Grind — homepage
+
+Static site served with `pnpm start`.
+
+## WebMCP tools
+
+`webmcp-tools.js` renders the Seasonal Favorites cards and the order tray from one
+menu dataset, and registers client-side tools through the WebMCP Imperative API
+(`document.modelContext.registerTool`). Registration is feature-detected, so
+browsers without WebMCP still get the menu and tray. WebMCP currently needs
+Chromium 146+ with `chrome://flags/#enable-webmcp-testing` and a secure context.
+
+| Tool | Effect | Annotations |
+|---|---|---|
+| `list_seasonal_favorites` | All seasonal drinks with per-size prices, tags, caffeine, availability | read-only |
+| `get_drink_details` | One drink plus an exact quote for a size and milk | read-only |
+| `filter_seasonal_favorites` | Filters and sorts the cards on the page; no args resets | mutates UI |
+| `highlight_drink` | Scrolls to and flashes a drink card | mutates UI |
+| `add_drink_to_order` | Adds a line to the on-page order tray | mutates UI |
+| `remove_drink_from_order` | Removes a line by id | mutates UI |
+| `get_current_order` | Current tray with line ids and total | read-only |
+| `place_order` | Opens a confirmation dialog; the order is only placed when the user clicks Confirm | `consequentialHint` |
+
+Errors are returned as `{ error, ... }` values rather than thrown so agents can
+self-correct. Ordering is simulated client-side; there is no backend call.
